## Test Anti-Pattern Audit — Severity-Ranked Findings

This is a textbook **"coverage-touching" test suite**. Every production method is called (→ 95% line coverage), but almost nothing is actually **verified**. Nine of ten tests would still pass if the production code returned garbage, deleted wrong records, or applied discounts backwards.

---

### 🔴 CRITICAL — Missing Assertions Entirely (tests prove nothing)

**1. `AddProduct_Works` (line 17)** — Fire-and-forget. No assertion that the product was actually persisted.
```csharp
// FIX:
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var saved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNotNull(saved);
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", saved.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, saved.Price);
```

**2. `UpdatePrice_Works` (line 32)** — Calls `UpdatePrice` but never checks the new price. Would pass even if price was unchanged or set to 0.
```csharp
// FIX:
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated!.Price);
```

**3. `RemoveProduct_Works` (line 38)** — Calls `RemoveProduct` but never checks the product is gone. Would pass if Delete was a no-op.
```csharp
// FIX:
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
```

**4. `GetProductCount_Works` (line 63)** — No assertion at all, and tests on an **empty catalog**, so it doesn't even exercise a meaningful path.
```csharp
// FIX:
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m));
_catalog.AddProduct(new Product("SKU-002", "Gadget", 19.99m));
Assert.AreEqual(2, _catalog.GetProductCount());
```

**5. `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (line 68)** — Applies a 10% discount but never checks any resulting price. A bug like `Price * (1 + fraction)` (markup instead of discount) would pass.
```csharp
// FIX:
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
var w = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(8.991m, w!.Price);   // 9.99 * 0.90
var g = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-002");
Assert.AreEqual(17.991m, g!.Price);  // 19.99 * 0.90
```

**6. `ImportFromCsv_Works` (line 84)** — Imports a CSV line but never checks that a product was actually created or parsed correctly.
```csharp
// FIX:
_catalog.ImportFromCsv("SKU-001,Widget,9.99");
var p = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
